feat(roster): render the public roster on team pages

The team page's own meta copy has always said it "shows the full roster,
schedule, results, upcoming games, recent news and venue information" —
but no roster was ever rendered. This adds it.

Source: `hockey_player_team_history` (the canonical roster-history table)
joined to `players`. 1,859 of those rows sit on active public teams — the
Toronto Maple Leafs alone have 44.

What renders:
- jersey number (red, dimmed past 99)
- player name, linking to /directory/players/{id}
- position when known
- a "COACH VERIFIED" marker for rows whose verification_source is
  "coach_verified". Self-reported rows are NOT badged — that is the
  default state, not a claim.
- the roster count

Data notes:
- the query is on supabaseAdmin because the players!inner(...) embed
  needs a relation whose RLS does not allow anon reads.
- rows with no matching player row are skipped rather than rendered blank.
- the section is hidden entirely when a team has no roster, so nothing
  changes for the long tail of teams without one.

Phase 2 of the roster build (Arnel: "Federations should be able to
update. Coaches and admins should be able to manage and accept payments.
Players should be able to manage their own passport.").
Next: league-page rosters, the team admin roster editor, and the
federation CSV upload.
